            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## Meso 0.3.0

The new Meso, rebuilt from the ground up. For now it runs on Macs with Apple silicon only.

**Coming from 0.2.4**
- The first time it opens, Meso brings over your settings, devices, buttons, keys, gestures and sequences, Time, usage statistics, Kindle export records and AI keys.
- Everything 0.2.4 wrote is kept untouched in `~/Library/Application Support/Meso/Backups/Meso 0.2`. To go back, install 0.2.4 again and move those files back.
- Not brought over: recipes, the menu bar layout, the downloader's list of past jobs, and a few actions the new Meso doesn't have yet.

**Since the last beta**
- Shelf: dropping a picture dragged from a web page no longer makes Meso quit.
- Plugins are ready as soon as Meso opens.
- Open App, used on the app that's already in front, hides it without reporting that it didn't open.
- Meso's log is much shorter.
]]></description>
